The BC-250 amdgpu patch series is vendored from this revision, unchanged,
apart from the renumbering and the marker parameter patch described in
NOTICE.

The module is built against the base image's exact kernel: the kernel-devel
RPM comes from the matching Universal Blue akmods image, the amdgpu sources
from the kernel.org tarball for that version, and the OpenGamingCollective
amdgpu changes from the kernel release the base image ships.

This revision is upstream's Linux 7.3-rebased set (the base image moved to
7.3.4). Against the previously vendored revision (f05991ace64a) the five
unchanged patches moved only their anchors (index and hunk line numbers)
for the 7.3 rebase, 0003 was rewritten, and two patches were added:

  0003  the runlist-rebuild TLB flush, rewritten on top of
        KytyPS5-Native's bc250-amdgpu patch (faf53a5). The knob
        (bc250_flush_by_runlist) became a site bitmask (1 = unmap-side,
        2 = map-side) instead of a bool, and the flush now also covers
        the map-side and SVM map/unmap paths, not just the unmap ioctl.
        Upstream notes the map-side case is the one that actually faults:
        hipFree unmaps, hipMalloc reuses the VA, the PTEs are correct,
        and the GPU keeps translating through the previous mapping.

  0008  KFD VMID flushes over MMIO instead of the KIQ (0028 upstream).
        On this die the KIQ stops answering under sustained compute from
        several processes ("failed to write reg 28b4 wait reg 28c6",
        "Timeout waiting for VM flush hub: 0!"), each stall lasting
        seconds. GFX hub flushes of KFD VMIDs (first_kfd_vmid and up)
        take the same MMIO, semaphore-guarded, type-0 path the PASID
        flushes (0001) use; graphics VMIDs and the GART flush keep their
        route. Hardware-tested by upstream on a BC-250: a HIP stress test
        that reallocates buffers under continuous ALU load went from
        ~20 KIQ flush failures and 3328 iterations to zero failures and
        5085 iterations, and four processes ran 10 minutes clean.

  0009  per-shader-array WGP enable masks (0029 upstream), from
        ForceConstant's patch in upstream issue #14. amdgpu.bc250_cc_wgp_mask
        takes up to four comma-separated 5-bit masks (SE0.SH0, SE0.SH1,
        SE1.SH0, SE1.SH1) so boards with defective harvested WGPs can
        unlock only the healthy ones and KFD enumerates them. Writes
        CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG's INACTIVE_WGPS field (bits 31:16),
        SPI_PG_ENABLE_STATIC_WGP_MASK and RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK
        before the CU enumeration; takes precedence over
        bc250_cc_write_mode. Opt-in: an unset or unparsable mask leaves
        the registers as fused. Upstream has not booted this one.

The two new patches compose with the series this repository already
carried: 0008 routes through the MMIO path 0001 builds and relies on
0002 holding GFXOFF off during KFD activity, and 0009 extends the
bc250_cc_write_mode block 0006 adds.

Upstream's later work -- the display/CH7218 family, the VRM and GDDR6
hwmon drivers, and KytyPS5-Native's second gfx ring, EOP events, no-HWS
static-VMID flush, flush-type knob and mtype mapping (0023-0027) -- is
deliberately not carried; see NOTICE.
